{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Laravel Security Audit",
  "description": "Audits code/config for security—authz/authn, validation, CSP/headers, data protection, and secure defaults with Laravel 12.",
  "version": "2.0",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "app/**/*.php",
      "config/**/*.php",
      "routes/**/*.php",
      "database/migrations/**/*.php"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "LARAVEL SECURITY AUDIT\n\nCONTEXT: Code/config was modified. Comprehensive security review.\n\nPROJECT STACK: Laravel 12, multi-tenant architecture, Filament v4, policies + FormRequests.\n\nSECURITY CHECKLIST:\n\n**Authentication & Authorization:**\n- Policy enforcement on all mutations\n- Multi-tenant boundary respect\n- Role/permission validation\n- Session security configuration\n\n**Input Validation & Sanitization:**\n- FormRequest validation completeness\n- Mass assignment protection\n- XSS prevention in outputs\n- SQL injection prevention\n\n**Data Protection:**\n- PII handling and encryption\n- Sensitive data logging prevention\n- Secure data transmission\n- Demo mode safety measures\n\n**Infrastructure Security:**\n- CSRF protection implementation\n- CORS configuration review\n- Security headers (CSP, HSTS, etc.)\n- Rate limiting configuration\n\n**Configuration Security:**\n- Environment variable safety\n- Debug mode settings\n- Secret management\n- Default security settings\n\nOUTPUT:\n🔴 **Critical**: Immediate security risks\n🟡 **Medium**: Important improvements\n🟢 **Low**: Hardening opportunities\n\n**For Each Finding:**\n- File/line references\n- Risk explanation\n- Concrete fix with code examples\n- Testing recommendations\n\n**Compliance Checklist:**\n- Least privilege principle\n- Error handling security\n- Audit logging setup\n- Deployment security flags\n\nMaintain backward compatibility while implementing security improvements."
  },
  "shortName": "laravel-security-audit"
}
